    <published>2026-09-08T17:30:00.000Z</published>
    <summary>一份集群生存指南：SLURM 调度、存储管理、环境优化与几条保命铁律。</summary>
    <title>HPC 集群折腾笔记：从 SLURM 到 48TB 家目录</title>
    <updated>2026-09-08T19:00:00.000Z</updated>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <author>
      <name>陈鑫宇</name>
    </author>
    <category term="Python" scheme="https://4choor3.github.io/categories/Python/"/>
    <category term="Python" scheme="https://4choor3.github.io/tags/Python/"/>
    <category term="自动化" scheme="https://4choor3.github.io/tags/%E8%87%AA%E5%8A%A8%E5%8C%96/"/>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<p>我不是计算机科班出身。第一次被 Python 吸引，是因为要整理一份三千行的实验记录表。手工复制粘贴到凌晨两点后，我写下人生第一行 <code>for</code> 循环，第二天十分钟跑完。那一刻我认定了一件事：<strong>凡是重复的事，就应该交给脚本。</strong></p><p>下面是我这几年慢慢攒下来的工具链，没有高深架构，全是能立刻上手的务实方案。</p><h2 id="数据处理：pandas-openpyxl"><a href="#数据处理：pandas-openpyxl" class="headerlink" title="数据处理：pandas + openpyxl"></a>数据处理：pandas + openpyxl</h2><p>我日常最多的重复劳动是和 Excel 打交道。pandas 读表、清洗、合并一气呵成，openpyxl 负责那些 pandas 不方便做的”细节活”——改单元格颜色、锁定表头、拆分多个 sheet。</p><figure class="highlight python"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line"><span class="keyword">import</span> pandas <span class="keyword">as</span> pd</span><br><span class="line"><span class="keyword">from</span> openpyxl <span class="keyword">import</span> load_workbook</span><br><span class="line"></span><br><span class="line">df = pd.read_excel(<span class="string">&quot;raw.xlsx&quot;</span>)</span><br><span class="line">clean = df.dropna().groupby(<span class="string">&quot;sample&quot;</span>).mean(numeric_only=<span class="literal">True</span>)</span><br><span class="line">clean.to_excel(<span class="string">&quot;summary.xlsx&quot;</span>, index=<span class="literal">False</span>)</span><br><span class="line"></span><br><span class="line"><span class="comment"># 用 openpyxl 补格式：冻结首行、加粗表头</span></span><br><span class="line">wb = load_workbook(<span class="string">&quot;summary.xlsx&quot;</span>)</span><br><span class="line">ws = wb.active</span><br><span class="line">ws.freeze_panes = <span class="string">&quot;A2&quot;</span></span><br><span class="line">wb.save(<span class="string">&quot;summary.xlsx&quot;</span>)</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>这套组合帮我把每周的报表从两小时压缩到跑一下脚本的功夫。</p><h2 id="自动化实战"><a href="#自动化实战" class="headerlink" title="自动化实战"></a>自动化实战</h2><h3 id="微信机器人（Wxauto-DeepSeek）"><a href="#微信机器人（Wxauto-DeepSeek）" class="headerlink" title="微信机器人（Wxauto + DeepSeek）"></a>微信机器人（Wxauto + DeepSeek）</h3><p>Mac 上的微信没有官方 bot 接口，我用 Wxauto 走 OneBot 协议接管客户端，再把收到的消息转给 DeepSeek 生成回复。核心就是个消息循环：</p><figure class="highlight python"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line"><span class="keyword">from</span> wxauto <span class="keyword">import</span> WeChat</span><br><span class="line"><span class="keyword">import</span> deepseek  <span class="comment"># 伪代码：调用模型接口</span></span><br><span class="line"></span><br><span class="line">wx = WeChat()</span><br><span class="line"><span class="keyword">while</span> <span class="literal">True</span>:</span><br><span class="line">    msgs = wx.GetListenMessage()</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="keyword">for</span> sender, text <span class="keyword">in</span> msgs:</span><br><span class="line">        reply = deepseek.chat(text)   <span class="comment"># 模型生成</span></span><br><span class="line">        wx.SendMsg(reply, sender)     <span class="comment"># 自动回</span></span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>它现在负责答复固定话术的客户，半夜也不再需要我爬起来回消息。</p><h3 id="Mac-GUI-自动化（cliclick-osascript）"><a href="#Mac-GUI-自动化（cliclick-osascript）" class="headerlink" title="Mac GUI 自动化（cliclick + osascript）"></a>Mac GUI 自动化（cliclick + osascript）</h3><p>有些老软件连 API 都没有，只能靠”模拟人点鼠标”。我用 <code>cliclick</code> 控制坐标点击，<code>osascript</code> 调 AppleScript 读写界面文本，串成一个脚本让 AI 接管日常操作：</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">cliclick c:120,80          <span class="comment"># 点击坐标</span></span><br><span class="line">osascript -e <span class="string">&#x27;tell app &quot;X&quot; to activate&#x27;</span></span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>真正的价值不在某一次点击，而是把”每天早上打开三个软件、导出一份数据”这种机械流程固化成一行命令。</p><h3 id="HPC：SLURM-上的长任务管理"><a href="#HPC：SLURM-上的长任务管理" class="headerlink" title="HPC：SLURM 上的长任务管理"></a>HPC：SLURM 上的长任务管理</h3><p>读生物信息时常要跑几小时甚至几天的比对任务。我在集群上用 tmux 保活会话，用 conda 隔离环境，再用脚本批量提交：</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">tmux new -d -s job1</span><br><span class="line">tmux send-keys -t job1 <span class="string">&#x27;conda activate bio &amp;&amp; python run.py&#x27;</span> C-m</span><br><span class="line">sbatch submit.sh   <span class="comment"># SLURM 调度</span></span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>重连时 <code>tmux attach</code> 一下就能看进度，断了网也不怕任务被 Kill。</p><h2 id="踩坑心得"><a href="#踩坑心得" class="headerlink" title="踩坑心得"></a>踩坑心得</h2><ol><li><strong>环境先于代码。</strong> 八成的”脚本跑不起来”是 Python 版本或依赖不对。我现在一律用 venv&#x2F;conda 锁环境，README 里写死版本。</li><li><strong>先能跑，再求美。</strong> 我大多先用最直白的写法把事办成，确认流程对了再重构。过早抽象反而是负担。</li><li><strong>留日志。</strong> 自动化跑在背后，出错你不一定知道。关键步骤 <code>print</code> 或写文件，至少能回头查”它到底干了啥”。</li></ol><p>工具链没有终点。每当一件事第二次要我动手，我就问自己：能不能写成脚本？久而久之，省下的不只是时间，更是那种”又得干重复活”的疲惫感。这大概就是我学 Python 最大的收获。</p>]]>
    </content>
